["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Palestine Is Not a National Cause but a Self-Reproducing Symbol-Extraction Machine Stop treating Palestine as a single national cause — inside the Middle East&#x27;s power structure it is a machine that converts suffering into an asset for every party involved: no centre, no king that could be killed, and no way out except clarity at the personal level. EconTalk EconTalk The Political Economy of Palestine (with Hussein Aboubakr Mansour) Middle East politics Rent-seeking Ideology Qatar Palestine Victimhood narrative autopoietic symbolic convertibility machine UNRWA teshuvah\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-03-econtalk-巴勒斯坦不是民族事业-而是自再生的政治经济榨取机器/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/f8da698e33560635-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:27:41</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">EconTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0803</span></div>\n<h2>Palestine Is Not a National Cause but a Self-Reproducing Symbol-Extraction Machine</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Stop treating Palestine as a single national cause — inside the Middle East&#x27;s power structure it is a machine that converts suffering into an asset for every party involved: no centre, no king that could be killed, and no way out except clarity at the personal level.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Middle East politics</span><span class=\"tag\">Rent-seeking</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Tungsten&#x27;s Price Spike Is a Hundred-Year War Prediction Market: China Cuts Supply and It Goes Up Tenfold Tungsten&#x27;s supply-and-demand cycle behaves like a war prediction market: prices spike before wars and collapse after them. China controls eighty percent of supply, and the West could restart old mines for only tens of millions of dollars — but with no futures market, the projects are hard to finance. Odd Lots Odd Lots The Tungsten Market Is Warning of an Upcoming War Tungsten Critical Minerals Geopolitics Supply Chains Mining Investment War Economy Ammonium Paratungstate (APT) Dry Metric Ton Unit (DMTU) Tungsten Carbide Ionic Absorption Clays\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-03-oddlots-钨价暴涨背后-一场百年战争预测市场/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">44:26</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0803</span></div>\n<h2>Tungsten&#x27;s Price Spike Is a Hundred-Year War Prediction Market: China Cuts Supply and It Goes Up Tenfold</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Tungsten&#x27;s supply-and-demand cycle behaves like a war prediction market: prices spike before wars and collapse after them. China controls eighty percent of supply, and the West could restart old mines for only tens of millions of dollars — but with no futures market, the projects are hard to finance.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Tungsten</span><span class=\"tag\">Critical Minerals</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"parent\" data-hay=\"The biggest financial gift to a child isn&#x27;t a college fund — it&#x27;s a business at 10 A 10-year-old earned $759 of retirement money from pet-sitting — not early hothousing, but real responsibility building systems thinking, boundaries, persistence and financial independence. Your Parenting Mojo Your Parenting Mojo Re-release: Raising an Entrepreneur (Without Taking Over Their Business) Kid entrepreneurship Financial literacy Roth IRA Self-directed learning Neurodiversity Hands-off parenting Roth IRA unschooling sliding scale pricing guide on the side intake form\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-03-parentmojo-给孩子最大的财务礼物不是大学基金-是让她10岁创业/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/70c340acb32275d2-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">1:00:19</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"parent\"><span class=\"src\">Your Parenting Mojo</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0803</span></div>\n<h2>The biggest financial gift to a child isn&#x27;t a college fund — it&#x27;s a business at 10</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A 10-year-old earned $759 of retirement money from pet-sitting — not early hothousing, but real responsibility building systems thinking, boundaries, persistence and financial independence.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Kid entrepreneurship</span><span class=\"tag\">Financial literacy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Regulating America&#x27;s Own AI Is Pointless Unless China&#x27;s Open Models Are Curbed Too If the US restrains only its own frontier models without suppressing China&#x27;s open models, the safety logic does not hold; the real decider is the compute stock and the ability to deliver. ChinaTalk ChinaTalk Jordan talks AI with Sebastian Mallaby on his show &#x27;The Spillover&#x27; US-China AI race Open weights Compute AI safety Export controls DeepSeek open weights distillation alignment tokenomics frontier lab\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-01-chinatalk-美国要慢可以-但得把中国开源一起管住/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/94fa934f85ccd79f-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">1:20:03</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\">ChinaTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0801</span></div>\n<h2>Regulating America&#x27;s Own AI Is Pointless Unless China&#x27;s Open Models Are Curbed Too</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">If the US restrains only its own frontier models without suppressing China&#x27;s open models, the safety logic does not hold; the real decider is the compute stock and the ability to deliver.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">US-China AI race</span><span class=\"tag\">Open weights</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Feishu and DingTalk Exit; the Personal Agent Takes Over AI Office Work Feishu is being folded into Doubao and DingTalk is ceding ground to Qwen Office (千问办公); enterprise IM has finished its historical mission. The center of AI office work shifts from organizational collaboration to individual productivity, with coding as the Agent&#x27;s foundation. 乱翻书 乱翻书 270.大厂押注AI办公，飞书和钉钉却先成了配角 AI Office Work Feishu DingTalk ByteDance Tencent Agents Agent ARR (Annual Recurring Revenue) CAPEX (Capital Expenditure) GEO (Generative Engine Optimization)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-01-luanfanshu-飞书钉钉退场-ai办公的主角成了个人agent/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/490e0c935e82c209-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"乱\"><span class=\"dur\">1:37:09</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">乱翻书</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0801</span></div>\n<h2>Feishu and DingTalk Exit; the Personal Agent Takes Over AI Office Work</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Feishu is being folded into Doubao and DingTalk is ceding ground to Qwen Office (<span lang=\"zh\">千问办公</span>); enterprise IM has finished its historical mission. The center of AI office work shifts from organizational collaboration to individual productivity, with coding as the Agent&#x27;s foundation.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI Office Work</span><span class=\"tag\">Feishu</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Dissected and Displayed After Hanging: What She Threatened Was Order, Not Money Mary Bateman, an 18th-century fraudster, worked through fortune-telling and a poisoned pie — not for the money, but for the pleasure of control. Her cons landed precisely on what people wanted to believe, and after her death her body was still put on display, exposing how much a society feared anyone who upended its order. Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford Cautionary Tales Arsenic and Lace: The Trial of the Yorkshire Witch - with Maddy Pelling Scams Psychological manipulation 18th century Historical crime Fraud defence Desire for power pleading the belly bottle conjurer ill wishes / well wishes\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-31-cautionary-约克郡女巫罪案-骗局的核心是权力欲/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b996da73a08744ac-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">43:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0731</span></div>\n<h2>Dissected and Displayed After Hanging: What She Threatened Was Order, Not Money</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Mary Bateman, an 18th-century fraudster, worked through fortune-telling and a poisoned pie — not for the money, but for the pleasure of control. Her cons landed precisely on what people wanted to believe, and after her death her body was still put on display, exposing how much a society feared anyone who upended its order.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Scams</span><span class=\"tag\">Psychological manipulation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"The Next Breakthrough in AI Research: Build a Physics of AI First, Then Let It Discover Architectures Itself Liu Ziming argues that real AFAI is not writing papers or rewriting training pipelines, but using the methods of physics to structure research first, then training a meta model to predict training curves, so that AI eventually discovers the next generation of architectures on its own. 张小珲·商业访谈录 张小珲·商业访谈录 149. 亲历中美neo labs资本狂潮，和清华刘子鸣聊：AI for AI、机制可解释性和Max Tegmark AI for AI Mechanistic Interpretability Meta Model Neo Labs Startup Fundraising Physics Thinking Physics of AI Mechanistic Interpretability Meta Model Recursive Superintelligence (RSI)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-30-zhangxiaojun-ai-for-ai-关键在于建立ai的物理学/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/ba3f758130e67a9c-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"张\"><span class=\"dur\">1:40:35</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">张小珲·商业访谈录</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0730</span></div>\n<h2>The Next Breakthrough in AI Research: Build a Physics of AI First, Then Let It Discover Architectures Itself</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Liu Ziming argues that real AFAI is not writing papers or rewriting training pipelines, but using the methods of physics to structure research first, then training a meta model to predict training curves, so that AI eventually discovers the next generation of architectures on its own.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>9</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI for AI</span><span class=\"tag\">Mechanistic Interpretability</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Brain Signals Show Up Seven Seconds Early, and the Researcher Still Says Free Will Survives The Libet and Haynes experiments show brain signals appearing half a second to seven seconds before ‘you decide’, but the researcher behind them denies this amounts to the absence of free will; compatibilism holds that will may be a macro-level emergent property of microscopic brain processes, the way temperature emerges from atoms. Science Vs Science Vs Free Will: Does It Exist? Free will Neuroscience Emergence Compatibilism Libet experiment Consciousness Emergence Clockwork universe fMRI (functional magnetic resonance imaging) EEG (electroencephalography)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-30-sciencevs-大脑早七秒做决定-自由意志依然存在/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/a3282246c3202bd6-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">31:49</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Science Vs</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0730</span></div>\n<h2>Brain Signals Show Up Seven Seconds Early, and the Researcher Still Says Free Will Survives</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The Libet and Haynes experiments show brain signals appearing half a second to seven seconds before ‘you decide’, but the researcher behind them denies this amounts to the absence of free will; compatibilism holds that will may be a macro-level emergent property of microscopic brain processes, the way temperature emerges from atoms.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Free will</span><span class=\"tag\">Neuroscience</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"For AI Application Companies, Surviving Beats Innovating: Liblib Turns Cash-Flow Positive An AI application company dismissed as ‘只会抄袭+投流’ — nothing but copying plus buying traffic — has been cash-flow positive since May, with paid advertising accounting for only 4% of revenue. Founder Chen Mian (陈冕): the era of applications has not arrived yet, and the most important goal is to stay alive; between being the first to find PMF and finally winning the market lies an enormous distance. 晚点聊 LateTalk 晚点聊 175: 对话Liblib陈冕：关于活下来，以及所有接近死亡的时刻 AI applications startup survival cash flow paid acquisition originality PMF / product-market fit Reward model LTV / lifetime value GTM / go-to-market AI native ARR / annual recurring revenue\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-30-latetalk-ai-应用公司的最优解是活下来-而不是创新/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/ff075962598c10e7-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"晚\"><span class=\"dur\">2:08:33</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">晚点聊 LateTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0730</span></div>\n<h2>For AI Application Companies, Surviving Beats Innovating: Liblib Turns Cash-Flow Positive</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">An AI application company dismissed as ‘<span lang=\"zh\">只会抄袭</span>+<span lang=\"zh\">投流</span>’ — nothing but copying plus buying traffic — has been cash-flow positive since May, with paid advertising accounting for only 4% of revenue. Founder Chen Mian (<span lang=\"zh\">陈冕</span>): the era of applications has not arrived yet, and the most important goal is to stay alive; between being the first to find PMF and finally winning the market lies an enormous distance.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI applications</span><span class=\"tag\">startup survival</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Tens of Thousands of Earthworks Under the Amazon, and a Civilization of Perhaps Three Million Using LiDAR to see through the rainforest canopy, archaeologists have found tens of thousands of earthworks in the southwestern Amazon, spread across more than 180,000 square kilometres, with a peak population that may have reached 3 million. Nature Podcast Nature Podcast Earthworks spotted in the Amazon hint at huge ancient civilization Amazon archaeology LiDAR Cephalopod fossils Fungal textiles Ancient civilizations Science findings LiDAR geoglyph siphuncle\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-29-naturepod-亚马逊地下古文明规模是预估的十倍/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/9b247947db171866-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"N\"><span class=\"dur\">20:30</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Nature Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0729</span></div>\n<h2>Tens of Thousands of Earthworks Under the Amazon, and a Civilization of Perhaps Three Million</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Using LiDAR to see through the rainforest canopy, archaeologists have found tens of thousands of earthworks in the southwestern Amazon, spread across more than 180,000 square kilometres, with a peak population that may have reached 3 million.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Amazon archaeology</span><span class=\"tag\">LiDAR</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Non-programmers Were Sneaking Into Codex, and ChatGPT Work Followed OpenAI handed knowledge workers the Codex harness essentially unchanged, altering only the UX trade-offs and the sandbox defaults. The judgment underneath: AI will erase the boundaries between job functions, so OpenAI refuses to draw product lines around &quot;who you are&quot;. Latent Space Latent Space Codex from 0 to 10M Users: Building ChatGPT Work — Akshay Nathan, OpenAI Agent product design Enterprise adoption Knowledge work Productivity metrics OpenAI harness artifacts Sites Chronicle at-bats OpenClaw\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-28-latentspace-chatgpt-work-与-codex-是同一个-harness-差的只是-u/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/ae9bcc0d8a995877-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:09:28</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Latent Space</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0728</span></div>\n<h2>Non-programmers Were Sneaking Into Codex, and ChatGPT Work Followed</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">OpenAI handed knowledge workers the Codex harness essentially unchanged, altering only the UX trade-offs and the sandbox defaults. The judgment underneath: AI will erase the boundaries between job functions, so OpenAI refuses to draw product lines around &quot;who you are&quot;.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Agent product design</span><span class=\"tag\">Enterprise adoption</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Intelligence will commoditize like RAM; OpenAI&#x27;s real moat is compute Sam Altman takes stock: intelligence itself will commoditize the way RAM did, and the durable advantage is the ability to manufacture cheaper compute. He also walks through ChatGPT&#x27;s accidental birth, the Hugging Face safety incident, and how the bottleneck keeps moving. Invest Like the Best Invest Like the Best Sam Altman - How to Make an Abundant Future - [Invest Like the Best, EP.484] Compute OpenAI Model cycle ChatGPT origins Commoditized intelligence Robotics distillation zero-day exploit Pareto optimal frontier scaling laws\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-28-ilt-智能终将商品化-openai-真正的护城河是算力/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/efc93bee38b040b6-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">53:33</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Invest Like the Best</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0728</span></div>\n<h2>Intelligence will commoditize like RAM; OpenAI&#x27;s real moat is compute</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Sam Altman takes stock: intelligence itself will commoditize the way RAM did, and the durable advantage is the ability to manufacture cheaper compute. He also walks through ChatGPT&#x27;s accidental birth, the Hugging Face safety incident, and how the bottleneck keeps moving.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Compute</span><span class=\"tag\">OpenAI</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Open models will win, and vLLM is the Linux of AI inference vLLM is already the most active open-source project on GitHub, but Kaichao You&#x27;s (游凯超) real claim is this: model capability cannot stay hidden for long, open models will win in the end, and the inference engine is the next Linux — where the moat is fast iteration, not the model itself. 张小珺·商业访谈录 张小珺·商业访谈录 148. 对游凯超3小时访谈：开源Infra、和模型Co-design 、“如果vLLM失败，我们会后悔一辈子” Open source AI Infra vLLM Model inference Startups Co-design PagedAttention KV Cache Speculative Decoding MOE (Mixture of Experts) BYOC (Bring Your Own Cloud)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-28-zhangxiaojun-开源模型会赢-vllm-是-ai-推理的-linux/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b00d9a408d39cab4-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"张\"><span class=\"dur\">3:00:26</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">张小珺·商业访谈录</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0728</span></div>\n<h2>Open models will win, and vLLM is the Linux of AI inference</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">vLLM is already the most active open-source project on GitHub, but Kaichao You&#x27;s (<span lang=\"zh\">游凯超</span>) real claim is this: model capability cannot stay hidden for long, open models will win in the end, and the inference engine is the next Linux — where the moat is fast iteration, not the model itself.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Open source</span><span class=\"tag\">AI Infra</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"AI Won&#x27;t Break SAP, But It Will Break Per-Seat Pricing AI will not flatten what enterprise software has accumulated, but it will break the per-seat pricing model. SAP&#x27;s defense is not training its own foundation model — it is open partnership plus business understanding, and the real battlefield is the last mile: process, data and organizational inertia. 晚点聊 LateTalk 晚点聊 174: AI冲击企业软件巨头？与SAP原欣聊大模型to B的颠覆与边界 Enterprise Software SaaS Pricing AI for B2B FDE SAP Organizational Inertia ERP / Enterprise Resource Planning FDE / Forward Deployed Engineer Human in the loop Process mining Physical AI\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-27-latetalk-企业软件不会死-死的是按坐席收费的模式/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/fd22b63fab892cb7-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"晚\"><span class=\"dur\">1:31:43</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">晚点聊 LateTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0727</span></div>\n<h2>AI Won&#x27;t Break SAP, But It Will Break Per-Seat Pricing</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI will not flatten what enterprise software has accumulated, but it will break the per-seat pricing model. SAP&#x27;s defense is not training its own foundation model — it is open partnership plus business understanding, and the real battlefield is the last mile: process, data and organizational inertia.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Enterprise Software</span><span class=\"tag\">SaaS Pricing</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Chinese superpods now out-compute NVIDIA in total, but 5x the power buys no ecosystem Huawei&#x27;s CloudMatrix 384 spends roughly 560 kW to deliver 1.7x the total compute of an NVL72, but what decides the fate of domestic superpods is not the spec sheet — it is manufacturing capacity and the software ecosystem. What&#x27;s Next｜科技早知道 科技早知道 国产 AI 算力能凭「超节点」弯道超车吗? | WAIC 深度观察 S10E23 Compute Superpods Domestic chips AI infrastructure NVIDIA Scale-up Scale-out UALink / Ultra Accelerator Link CloudMatrix / Huawei&#x27;s superpod line\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-27-whatsnext-国产超节点总算力反超英伟达-但功耗翻五倍换不来生态/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/98eaf4baa4b6920b-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"W\"><span class=\"dur\">47:23</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">What&#x27;s Next｜科技早知道</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0727</span></div>\n<h2>Chinese superpods now out-compute NVIDIA in total, but 5x the power buys no ecosystem</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Huawei&#x27;s CloudMatrix 384 spends roughly 560 kW to deliver 1.7x the total compute of an NVL72, but what decides the fate of domestic superpods is not the spec sheet — it is manufacturing capacity and the software ecosystem.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Compute</span><span class=\"tag\">Superpods</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Without Claude Code, Opus 4.5 Would Never Have Had Its Breakout Anthropic&#x27;s product lead looks back: however strong a model gets, users only feel it through a vehicle like Claude Code — and the core of the PM job has shifted from writing PRDs to writing evals. As she puts it, the eval is the new PRD. Lenny&#x27;s Podcast Lenny&#x27;s Podcast Anthropic’s first technical PM on token maxing, the jagged edge, and living in the future | Dianne Penn Product Management AI Research Orgs Evals Anthropic Culture Frontier Model Safety Token Economics token maxing jagged edge evals DRI red teaming hive mind\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-26-lennys-没有claude-code-opus-4-5不会有那波爆发/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2381cda2525bf028-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:33:50</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Lenny&#x27;s Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0726</span></div>\n<h2>Without Claude Code, Opus 4.5 Would Never Have Had Its Breakout</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Anthropic&#x27;s product lead looks back: however strong a model gets, users only feel it through a vehicle like Claude Code — and the core of the PM job has shifted from writing PRDs to writing evals. As she puts it, the eval is the new PRD.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Product Management</span><span class=\"tag\">AI Research Orgs</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"China Cut 5 Million Barrels a Day of Imports — Why the Iran Oil Apocalypse Never Came The Iran war was once forecast to push oil to $200 a barrel; the disaster never arrived, and the main reason was not the United States but China quietly cutting crude imports by 5 million barrels a day — discretion that can rescue a market, and can just as easily be turned into a geopolitical weapon. ChinaTalk ChinaTalk The Iran War Oil Shock That Wasn’t...(Yet?) Energy security US-China rivalry Strategic Petroleum Reserve Geopolitics Oil prices China policy SPR Exchange DUCs Apparent demand Malacca Dilemma\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-26-chinatalk-中国用5百万桶进口消失挡掉了伊朗油价末日/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/6a383006e06ec26c-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">1:06:00</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\">ChinaTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0726</span></div>\n<h2>China Cut 5 Million Barrels a Day of Imports — Why the Iran Oil Apocalypse Never Came</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The Iran war was once forecast to push oil to $200 a barrel; the disaster never arrived, and the main reason was not the United States but China quietly cutting crude imports by 5 million barrels a day — discretion that can rescue a market, and can just as easily be turned into a geopolitical weapon.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Energy security</span><span class=\"tag\">US-China rivalry</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"No One Confirmed the Doors Were Shut: Institutional Carelessness Was the Real Killer In 1987 the roll-on/roll-off ferry Herald of Free Enterprise capsized with her bow doors open, killing 193 people. The real culprit was not the sleeping crewman but a system that left everyone feeling this was not their job. Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford Cautionary Tales The Doors of Death: The Herald of Free Enterprise Maritime disaster Organizational failure Safety culture Accountability Regulatory lag Swiss cheese model roll-on/roll-off ferry (RoRo) Swiss cheese model corporate manslaughter controlling mind pacing problem\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-24-cautionary-没人确认舱门已关-制度性漫不经心才是元凶/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b996da73a08744ac-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">37:48</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0724</span></div>\n<h2>No One Confirmed the Doors Were Shut: Institutional Carelessness Was the Real Killer</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In 1987 the roll-on/roll-off ferry Herald of Free Enterprise capsized with her bow doors open, killing 193 people. The real culprit was not the sleeping crewman but a system that left everyone feeling this was not their job.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Maritime disaster</span><span class=\"tag\">Organizational failure</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"AI Only Gets You Because Content Engineers Coached It, Line by Line People who used to write the news have turned into AI&#x27;s content engineers, breaking questioning, empathy and a sense of proportion down into training rules — that is where AI&#x27;s ‘understanding’ of you comes from. But training on consensus also leads them to admit: great art will not grow out of this. 硅谷101 硅谷101 E245｜藏在大模型背后的新闻人：GPT们的回复是这样写出来的 Content Engineer Post-training AI Product Design Humanities Career Switch Large Models Generative AI Content Engineer System Prompt Few-shot Example Voice Agent Parasocial Relationship\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-24-sv101-ai的懂你-是内容工程师一句句调教出来的/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/cfe8fa9f8e3fa476-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"硅\"><span class=\"dur\">46:00</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">硅谷101</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0724</span></div>\n<h2>AI Only Gets You Because Content Engineers Coached It, Line by Line</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">People who used to write the news have turned into AI&#x27;s content engineers, breaking questioning, empathy and a sense of proportion down into training rules — that is where AI&#x27;s ‘understanding’ of you comes from. But training on consensus also leads them to admit: great art will not grow out of this.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Content Engineer</span><span class=\"tag\">Post-training</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Can a small model that grinds for eight weeks break the foundation-model oligopoly? With a model of 118 billion total parameters and 8 billion active, Poolside argues that persistence and verification behaviour lift coding ability more than raw parameter count does — which is why they believe small open models can break the incumbents&#x27; lock on the future. Latent Space Latent Space Inside the Model Factory — Eiso Kant, Poolside AI Open models Model training Reinforcement learning AI infrastructure AGI Compute RSI / recursive self-improvement MCP / Model Context Protocol FP8/NVFP4 / 8-bit and 4-bit low-precision training DGX Spark / NVIDIA desktop-class AI machine prefill/decode disaggregation\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-23-latentspace-poolside-小模型的持久性-比参数量更重要/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b0ae86616b939d17-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:54:33</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Latent Space</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0723</span></div>\n<h2>Can a small model that grinds for eight weeks break the foundation-model oligopoly?</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">With a model of 118 billion total parameters and 8 billion active, Poolside argues that persistence and verification behaviour lift coding ability more than raw parameter count does — which is why they believe small open models can break the incumbents&#x27; lock on the future.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Open models</span><span class=\"tag\">Model training</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Open models aren&#x27;t closing the gap by distilling — nobody knows how to distill usefully Nathan Lambert takes apart, point by point, the narrative that Chinese open models are just distilled: using Fable/GPT 5.6 as a judge inside the RL stage does not pencil out on cost, and even if you were handed the strongest model&#x27;s reasoning traces for free, the research community still does not know how to convert them into capability. Interconnects Interconnects Open models recap: more on Kimi K3, Qwen 3.8, Xi&#x27;s WAIC speech, distillation, the open-closed gap, and what&#x27;s next Open models Distillation Post-training Compute US-China rivalry Cybersecurity distillation rollout grading model / judge mid-training shadow ban fine-tunability\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-22-interconnects-开源追上前沿不是靠蒸馏-因为没人知道蒸馏怎么才管用/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b69e8536b2b28144-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">49:05</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Interconnects</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0722</span></div>\n<h2>Open models aren&#x27;t closing the gap by distilling — nobody knows how to distill usefully</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Nathan Lambert takes apart, point by point, the narrative that Chinese open models are just distilled: using Fable/GPT 5.6 as a judge inside the RL stage does not pencil out on cost, and even if you were handed the strongest model&#x27;s reasoning traces for free, the research community still does not know how to convert them into capability.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Open models</span><span class=\"tag\">Distillation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"A 28nm Chip Outruns the Leading Edge by 1,000x: Compute-in-Memory Black Magic Without EUV Zhicun Technology (知存科技) turned 28nm Flash into compute-in-memory chips. Because the physics make larger arrays more energy-efficient, efficiency rises as models get bigger — and Transformers are pure upside for the approach. 老石谈芯 老石谈芯 28纳米反超1000倍?不需要EUV的芯片黑魔法：对话知存科技王绍迪 Compute-in-Memory AI Chips Memory Transformer Semiconductor Manufacturing On-Device AI Von Neumann architecture NOR Flash NAND Flash EDA INT4 Universal Memory\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-22-laoshi-模型越大-28纳米存算芯片反而越强/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/83e6fe7e812c63f5-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"老\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">老石谈芯</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0722</span></div>\n<h2>A 28nm Chip Outruns the Leading Edge by 1,000x: Compute-in-Memory Black Magic Without EUV</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Zhicun Technology (<span lang=\"zh\">知存科技</span>) turned 28nm Flash into compute-in-memory chips. Because the physics make larger arrays more energy-efficient, efficiency rises as models get bigger — and Transformers are pure upside for the approach.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Compute-in-Memory</span><span class=\"tag\">AI Chips</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Three gates still stand between your agent and your money: trust, authorization, merchant readiness Clink and Visa completed the first agent payment, yet the industry is stuck at three gates — trust, authorization and merchant readiness; fiat is running first because consumer protection is mature, while stablecoins are still working on irreversibility. What&#x27;s Next｜科技早知道 科技早知道 可以给你的 Agent 发一点零花钱了 | S10E22 AI Agent Agent Payments Payment Protocols Visa Stablecoins Agent Payment ACP UCP / User Choice Protocol VIC / Visa Intelligent Commerce agent enableer chargeback\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-22-whatsnext-智能体支付已落地-但替你花钱还差三道坎/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/98eaf4baa4b6920b-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"W\"><span class=\"dur\">41:47</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">What&#x27;s Next｜科技早知道</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0722</span></div>\n<h2>Three gates still stand between your agent and your money: trust, authorization, merchant readiness</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Clink and Visa completed the first agent payment, yet the industry is stuck at three gates — trust, authorization and merchant readiness; fiat is running first because consumer protection is mature, while stablecoins are still working on irreversibility.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI Agent</span><span class=\"tag\">Agent Payments</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Embodied AI hasn&#x27;t reached its GPT-1 moment; the block is data that won&#x27;t scale Shen Yujun (沈宇军) of Ant Lingbo (蚂蚁灵波) argues embodied AI has not reached its GPT-1 moment, and the bottleneck is that data has not scaled up: internet data is two orders of magnitude larger than real-robot data, and an ideal pretraining run would start at a million hours. To get there the team rebuilt visual pretraining from scratch and insists on starting from real sensors. 张小珺·商业访谈录 张小珺·商业访谈录 147. 和蚂蚁灵波沈宇军聊：机器人原生基础模型、大脑和本体的关系、预训练与数据scale up、老师汤晓鸥 Embodied AI Robot brains Pretraining Data Ant Lingbo Founding a startup Ego (first-person-view) data WAM (world action model) VLA (vision-language-action model) MOE (mixture of experts)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-07-22-zhangxiaojun-具身数据没scale-up-gpt-1时刻就还没到/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/94df3a5e17c378cd-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"张\"><span class=\"dur\">1:52:54</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">张小珺·商业访谈录</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0722</span></div>\n<h2>Embodied AI hasn&#x27;t reached its GPT-1 moment; the block is data that won&#x27;t scale</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Shen Yujun (<span lang=\"zh\">沈宇军</span>) of Ant Lingbo (<span lang=\"zh\">蚂蚁灵波</span>) argues embodied AI has not reached its GPT-1 moment, and the bottleneck is that data has not scaled up: internet data is two orders of magnitude larger than real-robot data, and an ideal pretraining run would start at a million hours. To get there the team rebuilt visual pretraining from scratch and insists on starting from real sensors.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Embodied AI</span><span class=\"tag\">Robot brains</span>\n</div></div></a>"]